Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 46 CLINICAL DATA  Incision made into specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LYMPHOCYTIC MASTITIS  NOTE  An atypical epithelial proliferation is not identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 46 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is no staining  With antibody to B lineage antigen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    there is staining of most cells in a perivascular pattern  and associated with breast lobular ducts  The B cells are positive for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    there is staining of rare small cells scattered within the tissue  With antibody to cytokeratin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 cam 5 2   there is staining of epithelial cells  No lymphoepithelial lesions are identified  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results are suspicious for a low grade B cell lymphoma or B cell chronic lymphocytic leukemia  Additional studies that might help to provide a definite diagnosis include rebiopsy to obtain fresh frozen tissue for more optimal immunohistologic analysis  if clinically indicated  In addition  review of the peripheral blood with flow cytometric analysis for any evidence of monoclonal lymphoid population is also suggested  Added by  Phuong Nguyen  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 15 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Pro